<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan private machinery orders up 11.8 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan private machinery orders up 11.8 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's private-sector machinery orders, excluding those for machinery at electric power firms and for ships, rose a seasonally adjusted 11.8 percent in January from the previous month to 1.20 trillion yen, the Economic Planning Agency (EPA) said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Month-on-month percentage changes, seasonally adjusted, in different categories of machinery orders were as follows:</p>
<p>			JAN		 DEC</p>
<p>Overall	     +16.1	     -17.7</p>
<p> Private	    +11.8	     -12.8</p>
<p>(excluding ships, electric utilities)</p>
<p>			JAN		 DEC</p>
<p> Public	     -11.4	     -20.9</p>
<p> External	   +11.8	     -14.8</p>
<p>Year-on-year percentage changes, not adjusted for seasonal factors, in different categories of machinery orders were as follows:</p>
<p>			 JAN		DEC</p>
<p>Overall		+9.5		-0.8</p>
<p> Private	    +14.8		+0.2</p>
<p>(excluding ships, electric utilities)</p>
<p>			 JAN		DEC</p>
<p> Public	     -35.5	     -14.5</p>
<p> External	   +30.0	     +12.7</p>
</text>
